meta {
  name: 04_ResourceNotDelegable
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  Scenario: The resource delegation endpoints refuse a resource that cannot be delegated

    When another service owner looks up the rights for it the request fails as not delegable, not forbidden
    When another service owner delegates it the request fails as not delegable, not forbidden
    When the rights for a MaskinportenSchema resource are looked up the request fails
    When a MaskinportenSchema resource is delegated the request fails

  The Delegable flag is imported from the Resource Registry to the local resource
  (#4896, #4852), and the endpoints read it from there. The resource type and the
  Delegable flag rule a resource out whoever asks, so both are checked before ownership
  (#4842): a service owner that does not own the resource gets 400 AM-00042, not
  403 AM-00048.

  The resources are owned by ttd and have delegable=false in the Resource Registry. They
  must also be imported to Access Management; if a step returns 400 AM-00027 instead, the
  resource is missing locally.

  The owner being refused a non-delegable resource is covered by the k6 test
  service-owner-connections-not-delegable.js in altinn-platform-validation-tests, so this
  scenario only covers what that test does not: the check order against a service owner
  that does not own the resource, and the MaskinportenSchema type.

  None of the steps writes anything: every request is rejected before a delegation is
  created, so the scenario needs no reset or cleanup.
}
